diff --git a/docs/decisions/0069-retain-assistant-reservations-until-usage-is-known.md b/docs/decisions/0069-retain-assistant-reservations-until-usage-is-known.md
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..7dda776d
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/decisions/0069-retain-assistant-reservations-until-usage-is-known.md
@@ -0,0 +1,47 @@
+# Retain assistant reservations until usage is known
+
+Status: accepted for the staged PostgreSQL execution-budget component.
+
+## Context
+
+AGT-112 needs user and installation budgets that survive replicas and
+process restart. The assistant currently has deterministic commands and an
+installation execution policy, but no authoritative user allowance, model
+execution route or registered budget schema. Historical workspace cost
+reports cannot atomically admit concurrent assistant work.
+
+## Decision
+
+Reserve one execution and its finite worst-case token charge on both scopes
+in one borrowed PostgreSQL transaction. Recheck the current session and
+workspace before consulting a trusted policy source. Bind the reservation
+UUID to the exact execution digest, maximum charge and authenticated scope.
+Lock the reservation, installation counter and user counter in that order.
+Policy revisions reuse the same window counters.
+
+Only a newly committed reservation permits one execution. A held replay is
+pending and a settled replay is complete; neither grants another execution.
+An unknown commit returns no reservation. Reconcile the original UUID
+instead of retrying under a new identity.
+
+Keep a hold through timeout, cancellation, restart and window expiry.
+Settlement requires the original current authority, bounded actual usage
+and a stable digest of the trusted gateway receipt. Refund only unused
+tokens, once. Keep the admitted execution charged. Do not infer a refund
+from a missing reply, failed connection or model-generated usage.
+
+## Consequences
+
+A failed or uncertain execution can retain conservative capacity. Operator
+reconciliation needs its own authorized, audited contract; it cannot be an
+automatic time-based refund. An installation counter serializes writes to
+its current window, which is necessary for the first exact shared ceiling.
+
+The component introduces no alternative policy store or default allowance.
+Its DDL remains an isolated fixture input until the persistence owner adds
+a forward migration and restore catalogue. The gateway adapter must prove
+its maximum charge before admission. Human confirmation, effect permissions
+and success auditing remain the action owner's responsibilities. Loop
+limits, production binding, telemetry, controls and browser flows remain
+open in AGT-112. See the
+[research and verification contract](../research/product-assistant-execution-budgets.md).
diff --git a/docs/research/product-assistant-execution-budgets.md b/docs/research/product-assistant-execution-budgets.md
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..c5f9f42f
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/research/product-assistant-execution-budgets.md
@@ -0,0 +1,140 @@
+# Durable product assistant execution budgets (AGT-112)
+
+Reviewed: 2026-11-12. This is an implementation contract for the owned
+reservation boundary. Production configuration, route binding, loop limits
+and browser acceptance remain open. No policy is inferred from model output.
+
+## Sources and licences
+
+[Kubernetes resource quotas](https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/policy/resource-quotas/)
+apply aggregate limits when admitting work. Retrospective usage reports do
+not substitute for admission. The existing ownsolid metering budget preview
+reserves no capacity and has workspace, rather than user, scope.
+
+[PostgreSQL row locks](https://www.postgresql.org/docs/18/explicit-locking.html#LOCKING-ROWS)
+last until transaction completion. A waiting writer reads the updated row
+after its predecessor commits under
+[Read Committed](https://www.postgresql.org/docs/18/transaction-iso.html#XACT-READ-COMMITTED).
+[INSERT ON CONFLICT](https://www.postgresql.org/docs/18/sql-insert.html)
+establishes a unique reservation before charging either counter. Lock every
+reservation first, then installation and user counters in that fixed order.
+
+[LangGraph persistence](https://docs.langchain.com/oss/python/langgraph/persistence)
+uses persistent checkpoints for interruption and recovery. Its in-memory
+checkpointer loses state on restart. Budget reservations must likewise
+outlive the process admitting an action. A checkpoint alone cannot establish
+whether a remote effect happened after a lost reply.
+
+No dependency, model or dataset is added. The code reuses Go's
+[BSD-style standard library](https://go.dev/LICENSE), existing
+[pgx v5.11.0](https://github.com/jackc/pgx/blob/v5.11.0/LICENSE) under MIT,
+and [google/uuid v1.6.0](https://github.com/google/uuid/blob/v1.6.0/LICENSE)
+under BSD-3-Clause. The fixture reuses
+[PostgreSQL](https://www.postgresql.org/about/licence/) and
+[pgvector v0.8.7](https://github.com/pgvector/pgvector/blob/v0.8.7/LICENSE)
+under the PostgreSQL License. These terms permit commercial use, offline
+use and redistribution with applicable notices. LangGraph is a comparison,
+not a runtime dependency. Fixture identities and requests are synthetic.
+
+## Contract
+
+The command service's current installation policy remains the first
+execution gate. A separate trusted policy source must supply an explicit
+user enable decision, a stable UTC budget window, and finite installation
+and user ceilings for admitted executions and model tokens. An absent,
+unreadable or invalid policy is unavailable. Explicit user denial is forbidden.
+A zero ceiling means zero capacity, never unlimited capacity. No defaults,
+environment parser or second configuration store are introduced here.
+
+Recheck the real session and workspace in the owning transaction before
+reading policy or touching a reservation. Derive tenant, user and workspace
+from those server authorities. The browser and model cannot choose them.
+User counters span both entrances, tenants and every workspace for the same
+global user UUID; installation counters span the database. The trusted source
+must supply the same user ceiling for that UUID and window. Policy revisions do not reset
+usage. The policy owner must keep window boundaries stable across replicas
+and configuration changes. Use the database clock after acquiring counter
+locks to reject an expired or future window.
+
+A trusted adapter supplies a server-issued reservation UUID, a digest of
+the exact bounded execution, and its maximum total model-token charge.
+Deterministic commands may reserve zero tokens. One newly admitted
+execution permanently consumes one execution unit and holds the maximum
+tokens in both counters atomically. Check by subtraction to avoid signed
+integer overflow. Any refusal rolls back the new reservation and both
+counters. There is no tool execution inside this storage transaction.
+
+A repeated UUID with the same subject, entrance, workspace, digest and
+maximum charge returns the durable state without charging again. A
+different binding conflicts. Only a newly committed reservation permits
+the adapter to start one execution. A held replay is pending, not another
+permission to execute. A settled replay is already complete. A missing or
+failed commit response permits no execution; reconcile the same UUID.
+
+Settlement accepts only trusted, bounded actual usage and the digest of
+the authenticated gateway receipt. It changes held to settled once,
+returns unused tokens to both original windows, and keeps the execution
+unit charged. Repeating the same usage and receipt is idempotent; changed
+usage or receipt conflicts. Require the original authenticated scope for
+settlement. Revocation can leave a conservative hold; it cannot grant a
+refund. There is no automatic release on cancellation, timeout, restart,
+window expiry or missing usage. A new policy window cannot move an old hold.
+
+The reservation is internal admission state, not an executed product action
+and not a success audit. Existing action transactions still own permission,
+confirmation, effects and assistant audit attribution. Reservation admission
+does not authorize a write or replace its signed plan and human confirmation.
+
+## Alternatives rejected
+
+- Process-local counters cannot coordinate replicas or survive restart.
+- Counting audit events or historical cost reports races concurrent work
+  and cannot hold the worst-case charge before inference.
+- Blindly retrying after an unknown commit can start an effect twice.
+- Expiring a hold by time can refund work that completed without a reply.
+- Resetting usage on policy revision lets configuration changes bypass a
+  still-active window. Changing ceilings must reuse the same counters.
+- A new assistant-owned policy table or default allowance would compete
+  with the configuration owner's missing authoritative source.
+
+## Verification requirements
+
+Use real disconnected PostgreSQL transactions through independent service
+instances. Concurrent requests must never exceed either ceiling, including
+two different users sharing the installation ceiling. A denied request
+must leave no reservation, counter change, tool effect or success audit.
+Verify duplicate races, changed bindings, zero capacity, exact capacity,
+integer bounds, expired windows, cancellation while locked, transaction
+rollback, and a lost commit reply. Reopen state through a new instance and
+verify a held replay cannot execute again. Verify settlement races and
+changed receipts, and preserve the original window across policy rollover.
+Exercise revoked sessions and workspace, user and tenant isolation. Missing
+candidate schema must fail closed. The candidate DDL is fixture-owned until
+the persistence owner registers a forward migration and restore catalogue.
+
+The public endpoint, production migration, trusted policy source, gateway
+usage binding, run-loop bounds, operator controls and both browser entrances
+are separate integration requirements. AGT-112 remains unchecked until
+those complete the main flow and offline acceptance.
+
+## Integration surface
+
+`productagent.NewExecutionBudgets(commands, policySource)` borrows the
+existing command service and accepts no pool configuration. `Reserve`
+takes the server-authenticated actor and a `BudgetExecution`; `Settle`
+takes the same scope and a `BudgetSettlement`. The trusted adapter alone
+constructs execution and canonical receipt digests and token bounds. Do not
+expose these methods as an endpoint taking those values from a caller.
+
+The boundary uses existing public error codes: `RATE_LIMITED` (429),
+`ACCESS_DENIED` (403), `SERVICE_NOT_READY` and sanitized storage errors
+(503), `IDEMPOTENCY_CONFLICT` (409), `RESOURCE_NOT_FOUND` (404), and
+`VALIDATION_FAILED` (400). Scope mismatch does not disclose an existing
+reservation. Commit uncertainty preserves the existing transaction outcome
+and returns no newly admitted result. The generic HTTP rate fallback is not
+a promise that capacity will be available after that time.
+
+The [decision](../decisions/0069-retain-assistant-reservations-until-usage-is-known.md)
+records conservative recovery. Production registration must pair a forward
+migration and restore catalogue with the trusted policy and bounded adapter;
+creating the schema alone does not enable the gate or complete the feature.
diff --git a/services/control/internal/modules/productagent/README.md b/services/control/internal/modules/productagent/README.md
index 2ebb3fe9..c84992de 100644
--- a/services/control/internal/modules/productagent/README.md
+++ b/services/control/internal/modules/productagent/README.md
@@ -52,6 +52,40 @@ qualification still requires a live authenticated gateway route and
 positive capability evidence. See the
 [replay instructions and acceptance](../../../../../docs/research/product-assistant-model-qualification.md).
 
+## Execution budget reservation candidate
+
+`NewExecutionBudgets` borrows this service's current session, workspace and
+installation policy. Its separate trusted policy source supplies an explicit
+user decision, stable window and finite execution and token ceilings.
+`Reserve` charges installation and global-user counters atomically on
+PostgreSQL. Only a successfully committed `BudgetNew` permits the trusted
+adapter to start work. `BudgetHeld` means work may already have started;
+reconcile it rather than executing again. An error returns no reservation,
+including when the commit outcome is unknown.
+
+`Settle` needs the original authenticated scope and trusted usage receipt.
+It returns unused tokens once, keeps the execution charged and binds retries
+to the same usage and receipt digest. Timeouts and restarts retain holds.
+Neither method performs a product action or substitutes for the action's
+permissions, success audit or human confirmation.
+
+The [candidate DDL](testdata/execution-budget.sql) is installed only by the
+isolated repository test. It is not a production migration. Current command
+routes do not bind this budget candidate. A production migration and restore
+catalogue, authoritative typed policy source, bounded gateway adapter,
+run-loop guard, telemetry and both browser flows must be integrated before
+AGT-112 can ship. Do not accept a browser's or model's maximum token estimate.
+See the [contract and acceptance](../../../../../docs/research/product-assistant-execution-budgets.md).
+
+With the protected PostgreSQL repository fixture inputs selected as described
+below, run:
+
+```sh
+GOPROXY=off GOSUMDB=off go -C services/control test -p=1 \
+  -tags repository_integration -run '^TestDurableExecutionBudgets$' \
+  ./internal/modules/productagent -count=1
+```
+
 ## Tests
 
 ```sh
diff --git a/services/control/internal/modules/productagent/execution_budget.go b/services/control/internal/modules/productagent/execution_budget.go
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..7d4c4998
--- /dev/null
+++ b/services/control/internal/modules/productagent/execution_budget.go
@@ -0,0 +1,195 @@
+package productagent
+
+import (
+	"context"
+	"errors"
+	"time"
+
+	wire "github.com/Passion-Flow/ownsolid/api/datasets/v1"
+	"github.com/Passion-Flow/ownsolid/services/control/internal/modules/identity"
+	"github.com/Passion-Flow/ownsolid/services/control/internal/platform/database/transaction"
+)
+
+// BudgetAccess is an explicit trusted user policy, separate from installation policy.
+type BudgetAccess string
+
+const (
+	// BudgetAccessEnabled permits checking this user's finite allowance.
+	BudgetAccessEnabled BudgetAccess = "enabled"
+	// BudgetAccessDisabled denies admission regardless of remaining allowance.
+	BudgetAccessDisabled BudgetAccess = "disabled"
+)
+
+// BudgetCeiling bounds admitted executions and their total model tokens in one window.
+// Zero is zero capacity. There is no unlimited sentinel.
+type BudgetCeiling struct {
+	Executions int64
+	Tokens     int64
+}
+
+// ExecutionBudgetPolicy comes from the installation's trusted policy owner.
+// Window boundaries must remain stable across replicas and policy revisions.
+type ExecutionBudgetPolicy struct {
+	UserAccess   BudgetAccess
+	WindowStart  time.Time
+	WindowEnd    time.Time
+	Installation BudgetCeiling
+	User         BudgetCeiling
+}
+
+// BudgetSubject is resolved from current server authority before policy is read.
+type BudgetSubject struct {
+	TenantID, UserID, WorkspaceID, Audience string
+}
+
+// ExecutionBudgetPolicySource reads a complete local policy on the supplied
+// transaction, honors cancellation, and returns an error for an absent decision.
+type ExecutionBudgetPolicySource func(context.Context, transaction.Executor, BudgetSubject) (ExecutionBudgetPolicy, error)
+
+// BudgetExecution binds a server-issued UUID to one exact, bounded execution.
+// ExecutionSHA256 hashes the trusted adapter's canonical action, not model prose.
+type BudgetExecution struct {
+	ID              string
+	ExecutionSHA256 string
+	MaximumTokens   int64
+}
+
+// BudgetReservationState describes durable admission without authorizing a replay.
+type BudgetReservationState string
+
+const (
+	// BudgetNew permits one execution only after Reserve has committed successfully.
+	BudgetNew BudgetReservationState = "new"
+	// BudgetHeld means the execution may already have started; never execute it again.
+	BudgetHeld BudgetReservationState = "held"
+	// BudgetSettled means trusted usage has already settled this execution.
+	BudgetSettled BudgetReservationState = "settled"
+)
+
+// BudgetReservation is empty on every failed or uncertain transaction outcome.
+type BudgetReservation struct {
+	ID    string
+	State BudgetReservationState
+}
+
+// BudgetSettlement carries usage from an authenticated, trusted gateway receipt.
+// It must not be populated directly from browser input or model-generated text.
+type BudgetSettlement struct {
+	ID            string
+	ActualTokens  int64
+	ReceiptSHA256 string
+}
+
+// ErrBudgetExceeded means one of the current finite ceilings has no capacity.
+var ErrBudgetExceeded = errors.New("RATE_LIMITED")
+
+// ExecutionBudgets reserves shared PostgreSQL capacity using current session and
+// workspace authority. It owns neither connection configuration nor policy storage.
+// Production adapters must commit a new reservation before starting any work.
+type ExecutionBudgets struct {
+	commands *Service
+	policy   ExecutionBudgetPolicySource
+}
+
+// NewExecutionBudgets binds a reservation boundary to the existing command
+// service. A nil policy source makes admission unavailable; it never defaults on.
+func NewExecutionBudgets(commands *Service, policy ExecutionBudgetPolicySource) (*ExecutionBudgets, error) {
+	if commands == nil || commands.identity == nil || commands.applications == nil ||
+		commands.applications.Workspaces == nil || commands.applications.Workspaces.Identity != commands.identity {
+		return nil, errExecutionPolicyUnavailable
+	}
+	return &ExecutionBudgets{commands: commands, policy: policy}, nil
+}
+
+// Reserve rechecks current authority and atomically charges both finite ceilings.
+// Only BudgetNew allows the trusted adapter to start one execution. A held replay
+// or unknown commit must be reconciled using the original ID, never re-executed.
+func (b *ExecutionBudgets) Reserve(ctx context.Context, actor identity.Auth, execution BudgetExecution) (BudgetReservation, error) {
+	if !wire.ValidID(execution.ID) || !budgetDigest(execution.ExecutionSHA256) || execution.MaximumTokens < 0 {
+		return BudgetReservation{}, errors.New("VALIDATION_FAILED")
+	}
+	var result BudgetReservation
+	err := b.withSubject(ctx, actor, func(ctx context.Context, tx transaction.Executor, subject BudgetSubject) error {
+		if err := b.commands.admitExecution(ctx); err != nil {
+			return err
+		}
+		if b.policy == nil {
+			return errExecutionPolicyUnavailable
+		}
+		policy, err := b.policy(ctx, tx, subject)
+		if err != nil {
+			return errExecutionPolicyUnavailable
+		}
+		if policy.UserAccess == BudgetAccessDisabled {
+			return ErrCommandDenied
+		}
+		if !validBudgetPolicy(policy) {
+			return errExecutionPolicyUnavailable
+		}
+		result, err = reserveBudgetWithin(ctx, tx, subject, execution, policy)
+		return err
+	})
+	if err != nil {
+		return BudgetReservation{}, err
+	}
+	return result, nil
+}
+
+// Settle returns unused held tokens exactly once while keeping the execution
+// unit charged. Disablement does not prevent settlement of known usage. Missing
+// usage, cancellation and process restart never release a hold automatically.
+func (b *ExecutionBudgets) Settle(ctx context.Context, actor identity.Auth, settlement BudgetSettlement) (BudgetReservation, error) {
+	if !wire.ValidID(settlement.ID) || !budgetDigest(settlement.ReceiptSHA256) || settlement.ActualTokens < 0 {
+		return BudgetReservation{}, errors.New("VALIDATION_FAILED")
+	}
+	var result BudgetReservation
+	err := b.withSubject(ctx, actor, func(ctx context.Context, tx transaction.Executor, subject BudgetSubject) error {
+		var err error
+		result, err = settleBudgetWithin(ctx, tx, subject, settlement)
+		return err
+	})
+	if err != nil {
+		return BudgetReservation{}, err
+	}
+	return result, nil
+}
+
+func (b *ExecutionBudgets) withSubject(ctx context.Context, actor identity.Auth, fn func(context.Context, transaction.Executor, BudgetSubject) error) error {
+	if b == nil || b.commands == nil || ctx == nil || actor.Me.Workspace == nil ||
+		actor.Me.Audience != "admin" && actor.Me.Audience != "portal" {
+		return ErrCommandDenied
+	}
+	return b.commands.withSession(ctx, actor, func(ctx context.Context, tx transaction.Executor) error {
+		if tx.Dialect() != transaction.PostgreSQL {
+			return errExecutionPolicyUnavailable
+		}
+		w, err := b.commands.applications.Workspaces.ReadScopeWithin(ctx, tx, actor, actor.Me.Workspace.ID)
+		if err != nil {
+			return err
+		}
+		return fn(ctx, tx, BudgetSubject{TenantID: w.TenantID, UserID: actor.Me.User.ID, WorkspaceID: w.ID, Audience: actor.Me.Audience})
+	})
+}
+
+func validBudgetPolicy(p ExecutionBudgetPolicy) bool {
+	return p.UserAccess == BudgetAccessEnabled && !p.WindowStart.IsZero() && p.WindowStart.Before(p.WindowEnd) &&
+		p.WindowStart.Equal(p.WindowStart.Truncate(time.Microsecond)) && p.WindowEnd.Equal(p.WindowEnd.Truncate(time.Microsecond)) &&
+		p.Installation.Executions >= 0 && p.Installation.Tokens >= 0 && p.User.Executions >= 0 && p.User.Tokens >= 0
+}
+
+func budgetDigest(s string) bool {
+	if len(s) != 64 {
+		return false
+	}
+	for _, c := range s {
+		if !(c >= '0' && c <= '9' || c >= 'a' && c <= 'f') {
+			return false
+		}
+	}
+	return true
+}
+
+func budgetFits(used BudgetCeiling, ceiling BudgetCeiling, tokens int64) bool {
+	return used.Executions >= 0 && used.Tokens >= 0 && tokens >= 0 && used.Executions < ceiling.Executions &&
+		used.Tokens <= ceiling.Tokens && tokens <= ceiling.Tokens-used.Tokens
+}
diff --git a/services/control/internal/modules/productagent/execution_budget_repository.go b/services/control/internal/modules/productagent/execution_budget_repository.go
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..c1ca1fb2
--- /dev/null
+++ b/services/control/internal/modules/productagent/execution_budget_repository.go
@@ -0,0 +1,158 @@
+package productagent
+
+import (
+	"context"
+	"database/sql"
+	"errors"
+	"time"
+
+	"github.com/Passion-Flow/ownsolid/services/control/internal/platform/database/transaction"
+)
+
+type budgetWindow struct{ start, end time.Time }
+
+type storedBudgetReservation struct {
+	execution BudgetExecution
+	window    budgetWindow
+	state     BudgetReservationState
+	actual    sql.NullInt64
+	receipt   sql.NullString
+}
+
+func budgetSQL(query string, args ...any) transaction.Statement {
+	return transaction.SQL(transaction.PostgreSQL, query, args...)
+}
+
+func reserveBudgetWithin(ctx context.Context, tx transaction.Executor, subject BudgetSubject, execution BudgetExecution, policy ExecutionBudgetPolicy) (BudgetReservation, error) {
+	n, err := tx.Exec(ctx, budgetSQL(`INSERT INTO product_agent_budget_reservations
+		(id,tenant_id,user_id,workspace_id,audience,execution_sha256,maximum_tokens,window_start,window_end,state)
+		VALUES($1,$2,$3,$4,$5,$6,$7,$8,$9,'held') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING`,
+		execution.ID, subject.TenantID, subject.UserID, subject.WorkspaceID, subject.Audience,
+		execution.ExecutionSHA256, execution.MaximumTokens, policy.WindowStart, policy.WindowEnd))
+	if err != nil {
+		return BudgetReservation{}, err
+	}
+	if n == 0 {
+		stored, err := readBudgetReservation(ctx, tx, subject, execution.ID)
+		if err != nil {
+			return BudgetReservation{}, err
+		}
+		if stored.execution != execution {
+			return BudgetReservation{}, errors.New("IDEMPOTENCY_CONFLICT")
+		}
+		return BudgetReservation{ID: execution.ID, State: stored.state}, nil
+	}
+	w := budgetWindow{policy.WindowStart, policy.WindowEnd}
+	used, err := lockBudgetCounters(ctx, tx, subject, w, true)
+	if err != nil {
+		return BudgetReservation{}, err
+	}
+	var current bool
+	if err := tx.QueryRow(ctx, budgetSQL(`SELECT $1::timestamptz <= statement_timestamp() AND statement_timestamp() < $2::timestamptz`, w.start, w.end)).Scan(&current); err != nil {
+		return BudgetReservation{}, err
+	}
+	if !current {
+		return BudgetReservation{}, errExecutionPolicyUnavailable
+	}
+	if !budgetFits(used[0], policy.Installation, execution.MaximumTokens) || !budgetFits(used[1], policy.User, execution.MaximumTokens) {
+		return BudgetReservation{}, ErrBudgetExceeded
+	}
+	if err := changeBudgetCounters(ctx, tx, subject, w, 1, execution.MaximumTokens); err != nil {
+		return BudgetReservation{}, err
+	}
+	return BudgetReservation{ID: execution.ID, State: BudgetNew}, nil
+}
+
+func readBudgetReservation(ctx context.Context, tx transaction.Executor, subject BudgetSubject, id string) (storedBudgetReservation, error) {
+	var stored storedBudgetReservation
+	stored.execution.ID = id
+	err := tx.QueryRow(ctx, budgetSQL(`SELECT execution_sha256,maximum_tokens,window_start,window_end,state,actual_tokens,receipt_sha256
+		FROM product_agent_budget_reservations WHERE id=$1 AND tenant_id=$2 AND user_id=$3 AND workspace_id=$4 AND audience=$5 FOR UPDATE`,
+		id, subject.TenantID, subject.UserID, subject.WorkspaceID, subject.Audience)).Scan(
+		&stored.execution.ExecutionSHA256, &stored.execution.MaximumTokens, &stored.window.start, &stored.window.end,
+		&stored.state, &stored.actual, &stored.receipt)
+	if errors.Is(err, sql.ErrNoRows) {
+		return storedBudgetReservation{}, errors.New("RESOURCE_NOT_FOUND")
+	}
+	return stored, err
+}
+
+func settleBudgetWithin(ctx context.Context, tx transaction.Executor, subject BudgetSubject, settlement BudgetSettlement) (BudgetReservation, error) {
+	stored, err := readBudgetReservation(ctx, tx, subject, settlement.ID)
+	if err != nil {
+		return BudgetReservation{}, err
+	}
+	if settlement.ActualTokens > stored.execution.MaximumTokens {
+		return BudgetReservation{}, errors.New("VALIDATION_FAILED")
+	}
+	result := BudgetReservation{ID: settlement.ID, State: BudgetSettled}
+	if stored.state == BudgetSettled {
+		if !stored.actual.Valid || !stored.receipt.Valid || stored.actual.Int64 != settlement.ActualTokens || stored.receipt.String != settlement.ReceiptSHA256 {
+			return BudgetReservation{}, errors.New("IDEMPOTENCY_CONFLICT")
+		}
+		return result, nil
+	}
+	if stored.state != BudgetHeld || stored.actual.Valid || stored.receipt.Valid {
+		return BudgetReservation{}, errExecutionPolicyUnavailable
+	}
+	used, err := lockBudgetCounters(ctx, tx, subject, stored.window, false)
+	if err != nil {
+		return BudgetReservation{}, err
+	}
+	for _, counter := range used {
+		if counter.Executions < 1 || counter.Tokens < stored.execution.MaximumTokens {
+			return BudgetReservation{}, errExecutionPolicyUnavailable
+		}
+	}
+	// Keep the execution charged even when the gateway proved zero token usage.
+	if err := changeBudgetCounters(ctx, tx, subject, stored.window, 0, settlement.ActualTokens-stored.execution.MaximumTokens); err != nil {
+		return BudgetReservation{}, err
+	}
+	n, err := tx.Exec(ctx, budgetSQL(`UPDATE product_agent_budget_reservations SET state='settled',actual_tokens=$2,receipt_sha256=$3
+		WHERE id=$1 AND state='held'`, settlement.ID, settlement.ActualTokens, settlement.ReceiptSHA256))
+	if err != nil {
+		return BudgetReservation{}, err
+	}
+	if n != 1 {
+		return BudgetReservation{}, errExecutionPolicyUnavailable
+	}
+	return result, nil
+}
+
+// The fixed installation-before-user order is shared by admission and settlement.
+func lockBudgetCounters(ctx context.Context, tx transaction.Executor, subject BudgetSubject, w budgetWindow, create bool) ([2]BudgetCeiling, error) {
+	var used [2]BudgetCeiling
+	for i := range used {
+		insert := budgetSQL(`INSERT INTO product_agent_budget_installations(window_start,window_end) VALUES($1,$2) ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING`, w.start, w.end)
+		read := budgetSQL(`SELECT executions,tokens FROM product_agent_budget_installations WHERE window_start=$1 AND window_end=$2 FOR UPDATE`, w.start, w.end)
+		if i == 1 {
+			insert = budgetSQL(`INSERT INTO product_agent_budget_users(user_id,window_start,window_end) VALUES($1,$2,$3) ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING`, subject.UserID, w.start, w.end)
+			read = budgetSQL(`SELECT executions,tokens FROM product_agent_budget_users WHERE user_id=$1 AND window_start=$2 AND window_end=$3 FOR UPDATE`, subject.UserID, w.start, w.end)
+		}
+		if create {
+			if _, err := tx.Exec(ctx, insert); err != nil {
+				return [2]BudgetCeiling{}, err
+			}
+		}
+		if err := tx.QueryRow(ctx, read).Scan(&used[i].Executions, &used[i].Tokens); err != nil {
+			return [2]BudgetCeiling{}, err
+		}
+	}
+	return used, nil
+}
+
+func changeBudgetCounters(ctx context.Context, tx transaction.Executor, subject BudgetSubject, w budgetWindow, executions, tokens int64) error {
+	for _, query := range []transaction.Statement{
+		budgetSQL(`UPDATE product_agent_budget_installations SET executions=executions+$3,tokens=tokens+$4 WHERE window_start=$1 AND window_end=$2`, w.start, w.end, executions, tokens),
+		budgetSQL(`UPDATE product_agent_budget_users SET executions=executions+$4,tokens=tokens+$5 WHERE user_id=$1 AND window_start=$2 AND window_end=$3`, subject.UserID, w.start, w.end, executions, tokens),
+	} {
+		n, err := tx.Exec(ctx, query)
+		if err != nil {
+			return err
+		}
+		if n != 1 {
+			return errExecutionPolicyUnavailable
+		}
+	}
+	return nil
+}
diff --git a/services/control/internal/modules/productagent/execution_budget_repository_integration_test.go b/services/control/internal/modules/productagent/execution_budget_repository_integration_test.go
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..b3c987fe
--- /dev/null
+++ b/services/control/internal/modules/productagent/execution_budget_repository_integration_test.go
@@ -0,0 +1,536 @@
+//go:build repository_integration
+
+package productagent
+
+import (
+	"context"
+	_ "embed"
+	"errors"
+	"math"
+	"strings"
+	"sync"
+	"sync/atomic"
+	"testing"
+	"time"
+
+	"github.com/Passion-Flow/ownsolid/services/control/internal/modules/applications"
+	"github.com/Passion-Flow/ownsolid/services/control/internal/modules/identity"
+	"github.com/Passion-Flow/ownsolid/services/control/internal/modules/workspaces"
+	"github.com/Passion-Flow/ownsolid/services/control/internal/platform/database/transaction"
+	"github.com/Passion-Flow/ownsolid/services/control/internal/testing/repositoryfixture"
+	"github.com/google/uuid"
+	"github.com/jackc/pgx/v5/pgxpool"
+)
+
+//go:embed testdata/execution-budget.sql
+var executionBudgetSchema string
+
+type budgetRepositoryFixture struct {
+	t           *testing.T
+	f           repositoryfixture.Fixture
+	ctx         context.Context
+	policy      atomic.Pointer[ExecutionBudgetPolicy]
+	actors      [3]identity.Auth
+	gates       [2]*ExecutionBudgets
+	replicaPool *pgxpool.Pool
+}
+
+func newBudgetRepositoryFixture(t *testing.T) *budgetRepositoryFixture {
+	t.Helper()
+	f := repositoryfixture.New(t)
+	if f.PostgreSQL == nil {
+		t.Skip("Durable assistant reservations require PostgreSQL")
+	}
+	ctx, cancel := context.WithTimeout(t.Context(), 120*time.Second)
+	t.Cleanup(cancel)
+	g := &budgetRepositoryFixture{t: t, f: f, ctx: ctx}
+	if _, err := f.PostgreSQL.Exec(ctx, executionBudgetSchema); err != nil {
+		t.Fatal(err)
+	}
+	owner := &identity.Service{Storage: f.Store}
+	for i, audience := range []string{"admin", "portal", "portal"} {
+		user := f.User
+		if i == 2 {
+			user = uuid.NewString()
+			email := user + "@example.invalid"
+			g.exec(`INSERT INTO users(id,email_canonical,email_display,display_name,locale,status,is_platform_admin) VALUES($1,$2,$2,'Budget second user','en','active',false)`, user, email)
+		}
+		if i != 1 {
+			g.exec(`INSERT INTO workspace_memberships(user_id,tenant_id,workspace_id,role,authority_id) VALUES($1,$2,$3,'owner',$4)`, user, f.Tenant, f.Workspace, uuid.NewString())
+		}
+		var issued identity.IssuedSession
+		if err := f.Store.Within(ctx, false, func(ctx context.Context, tx transaction.Executor) error {
+			var err error
+			issued, err = owner.IssueSessionWithin(ctx, tx, user, 1, audience, "", uuid.NewString(), nil)
+			return err
+		}); err != nil {
+			t.Fatal(err)
+		}
+		actor, err := owner.Authenticate(ctx, issued.Token, audience)
+		if err != nil || actor.Me.Workspace == nil || actor.Me.Workspace.ID != f.Workspace {
+			t.Fatalf("budget fixture authentication: %v", err)
+		}
+		g.actors[i] = actor
+	}
+	config := f.PostgreSQL.Config()
+	config.ConnConfig.RuntimeParams["application_name"] = "assistant-budget-" + uuid.NewString()
+	pool, err := pgxpool.NewWithConfig(ctx, config)
+	if err != nil {
+		t.Fatal(err)
+	}
+	t.Cleanup(pool.Close)
+	g.replicaPool = pool
+	replica, err := transaction.FromPostgreSQL(pool)
+	if err != nil {
+		t.Fatal(err)
+	}
+	g.gates[0] = g.gate(f.Store)
+	g.gates[1] = g.gate(replica)
+	g.reset(t)
+	return g
+}
+
+func (g *budgetRepositoryFixture) gate(store transaction.Store) *ExecutionBudgets {
+	g.t.Helper()
+	owner := &identity.Service{Storage: store}
+	apps := &applications.Service{Identity: owner, Workspaces: &workspaces.Service{Identity: owner}}
+	commands, err := New(apps, func(context.Context) (bool, error) { return true, nil })
+	if err != nil {
+		g.t.Fatal(err)
+	}
+	gate, err := NewExecutionBudgets(commands, func(context.Context, transaction.Executor, BudgetSubject) (ExecutionBudgetPolicy, error) {
+		return *g.policy.Load(), nil
+	})
+	if err != nil {
+		g.t.Fatal(err)
+	}
+	return gate
+}
+
+func (g *budgetRepositoryFixture) exec(query string, args ...any) {
+	g.t.Helper()
+	if _, err := g.f.PostgreSQL.Exec(g.ctx, query, args...); err != nil {
+		g.t.Fatal(err)
+	}
+}
+
+func (g *budgetRepositoryFixture) reset(t *testing.T) {
+	g.t = t
+	g.t.Helper()
+	g.exec(`TRUNCATE product_agent_budget_reservations,product_agent_budget_users,product_agent_budget_installations`)
+	start := time.Now().UTC().Truncate(time.Hour).Add(-time.Hour)
+	g.policy.Store(&ExecutionBudgetPolicy{
+		UserAccess: BudgetAccessEnabled, WindowStart: start, WindowEnd: start.Add(3 * time.Hour),
+		Installation: BudgetCeiling{100, 1000}, User: BudgetCeiling{100, 1000},
+	})
+}
+
+func (g *budgetRepositoryFixture) counters(user string, want BudgetCeiling, reservations int) {
+	g.t.Helper()
+	var got BudgetCeiling
+	p := g.policy.Load()
+	query := `SELECT executions,tokens FROM product_agent_budget_installations WHERE window_start=$1 AND window_end=$2`
+	args := []any{p.WindowStart, p.WindowEnd}
+	if user != "" {
+		query = `SELECT executions,tokens FROM product_agent_budget_users WHERE user_id=$3 AND window_start=$1 AND window_end=$2`
+		args = append(args, user)
+	}
+	if err := g.f.PostgreSQL.QueryRow(g.ctx, query, args...).Scan(&got.Executions, &got.Tokens); err != nil || got != want {
+		g.t.Fatalf("durable counters %+v, want %+v: %v", got, want, err)
+	}
+	var count int
+	if err := g.f.PostgreSQL.QueryRow(g.ctx, `SELECT count(*) FROM product_agent_budget_reservations`).Scan(&count); err != nil || count != reservations {
+		g.t.Fatalf("durable reservation count %d, want %d: %v", count, reservations, err)
+	}
+}
+
+func budgetTestExecution(tokens int64) BudgetExecution {
+	return BudgetExecution{ID: uuid.NewString(), ExecutionSHA256: strings.Repeat("a", 64), MaximumTokens: tokens}
+}
+
+type budgetTestOutcome struct {
+	reservation BudgetReservation
+	err         error
+}
+
+func concurrentBudgetCalls(n int, call func(int) (BudgetReservation, error)) []budgetTestOutcome {
+	results := make([]budgetTestOutcome, n)
+	start := make(chan struct{})
+	var workers sync.WaitGroup
+	for i := range n {
+		workers.Go(func() {
+			<-start
+			results[i].reservation, results[i].err = call(i)
+		})
+	}
+	close(start)
+	workers.Wait()
+	return results
+}
+
+func TestDurableExecutionBudgets(t *testing.T) {
+	g := newBudgetRepositoryFixture(t)
+	for _, tc := range []struct {
+		name       string
+		ceiling    BudgetCeiling
+		actors     []identity.Auth
+		userScoped bool
+	}{
+		{"user ceiling across entrances", BudgetCeiling{3, 6}, g.actors[:2], true},
+		{"installation ceiling across users", BudgetCeiling{4, 8}, g.actors[1:], false},
+	} {
+		t.Run(tc.name, func(t *testing.T) {
+			g.reset(t)
+			p := *g.policy.Load()
+			if tc.userScoped {
+				p.User = tc.ceiling
+			} else {
+				p.Installation = tc.ceiling
+			}
+			g.policy.Store(&p)
+			results := concurrentBudgetCalls(16, func(i int) (BudgetReservation, error) {
+				return g.gates[i%2].Reserve(g.ctx, tc.actors[i%len(tc.actors)], budgetTestExecution(2))
+			})
+			admitted := int64(0)
+			for _, result := range results {
+				if result.err == nil && result.reservation.State == BudgetNew {
+					admitted++
+				} else if result.err != ErrBudgetExceeded || result.reservation != (BudgetReservation{}) {
+					t.Fatalf("concurrent admission: %+v, %v", result.reservation, result.err)
+				}
+			}
+			if admitted != tc.ceiling.Executions {
+				t.Fatalf("admitted %d, want %d", admitted, tc.ceiling.Executions)
+			}
+			g.counters("", tc.ceiling, int(admitted))
+			if tc.userScoped {
+				g.counters(g.f.User, tc.ceiling, int(admitted))
+			}
+		})
+	}
+
+	t.Run("duplicate binding and settlement races", func(t *testing.T) {
+		g.reset(t)
+		execution := budgetTestExecution(7)
+		newCount := 0
+		for _, result := range concurrentBudgetCalls(12, func(i int) (BudgetReservation, error) {
+			return g.gates[i%2].Reserve(g.ctx, g.actors[1], execution)
+		}) {
+			if result.err != nil || result.reservation.ID != execution.ID {
+				t.Fatalf("duplicate admission: %+v, %v", result.reservation, result.err)
+			}
+			switch result.reservation.State {
+			case BudgetNew:
+				newCount++
+			case BudgetHeld:
+			default:
+				t.Fatalf("unexpected duplicate state: %s", result.reservation.State)
+			}
+		}
+		if newCount != 1 {
+			t.Fatalf("duplicate identity admitted %d executions", newCount)
+		}
+		g.counters("", BudgetCeiling{1, 7}, 1)
+		changed := execution
+		changed.ExecutionSHA256 = strings.Repeat("b", 64)
+		g.refusal(t, g.gates[0], g.actors[1], changed, "IDEMPOTENCY_CONFLICT")
+		changed = execution
+		changed.MaximumTokens++
+		g.refusal(t, g.gates[0], g.actors[1], changed, "IDEMPOTENCY_CONFLICT")
+		g.refusal(t, g.gates[1], g.actors[0], execution, "RESOURCE_NOT_FOUND")
+		g.refusal(t, g.gates[1], g.actors[2], execution, "RESOURCE_NOT_FOUND")
+		if result, err := g.gates[0].Settle(g.ctx, g.actors[1], BudgetSettlement{ID: execution.ID, ActualTokens: 8, ReceiptSHA256: strings.Repeat("c", 64)}); result != (BudgetReservation{}) || err == nil || err.Error() != "VALIDATION_FAILED" {
+			t.Fatalf("usage above the reserved maximum: %+v, %v", result, err)
+		}
+		settlement := BudgetSettlement{ID: execution.ID, ActualTokens: 2, ReceiptSHA256: strings.Repeat("c", 64)}
+		for _, result := range concurrentBudgetCalls(12, func(i int) (BudgetReservation, error) {
+			return g.gates[i%2].Settle(g.ctx, g.actors[1], settlement)
+		}) {
+			if result.err != nil || result.reservation != (BudgetReservation{execution.ID, BudgetSettled}) {
+				t.Fatalf("settlement race: %+v, %v", result.reservation, result.err)
+			}
+		}
+		g.counters("", BudgetCeiling{1, 2}, 1)
+		g.counters(g.f.User, BudgetCeiling{1, 2}, 1)
+		for _, changed := range []BudgetSettlement{
+			{ID: execution.ID, ActualTokens: 3, ReceiptSHA256: settlement.ReceiptSHA256},
+			{ID: execution.ID, ActualTokens: 2, ReceiptSHA256: strings.Repeat("d", 64)},
+		} {
+			if result, err := g.gates[0].Settle(g.ctx, g.actors[1], changed); err == nil || err.Error() != "IDEMPOTENCY_CONFLICT" || result != (BudgetReservation{}) {
+				t.Fatalf("changed settlement: %+v, %v", result, err)
+			}
+		}
+		if result, err := g.gates[1].Reserve(g.ctx, g.actors[1], execution); err != nil || result.State != BudgetSettled {
+			t.Fatalf("completed reservation replay: %+v, %v", result, err)
+		}
+		g.counters("", BudgetCeiling{1, 2}, 1)
+	})
+
+	t.Run("policy unavailable disabled and recovered", func(t *testing.T) {
+		g.reset(t)
+		gate := *g.gates[0]
+		for _, source := range []ExecutionBudgetPolicySource{
+			nil,
+			func(context.Context, transaction.Executor, BudgetSubject) (ExecutionBudgetPolicy, error) {
+				return ExecutionBudgetPolicy{}, errors.New("private policy diagnostic")
+			},
+			func(context.Context, transaction.Executor, BudgetSubject) (ExecutionBudgetPolicy, error) {
+				return ExecutionBudgetPolicy{}, nil
+			},
+		} {
+			gate.policy = source
+			g.refusal(t, &gate, g.actors[1], budgetTestExecution(1), "SERVICE_NOT_READY")
+		}
+		gate.policy = g.gates[0].policy
+		commands := *gate.commands
+		commands.executionPolicy = func(context.Context) (bool, error) { return false, nil }
+		gate.commands = &commands
+		g.refusal(t, &gate, g.actors[1], budgetTestExecution(1), "ACCESS_DENIED")
+		commands.executionPolicy = func(context.Context) (bool, error) { return true, errors.New("private installation diagnostic") }
+		g.refusal(t, &gate, g.actors[1], budgetTestExecution(1), "SERVICE_NOT_READY")
+		gate.commands = g.gates[0].commands
+		p := *g.policy.Load()
+		p.UserAccess = BudgetAccessDisabled
+		g.policy.Store(&p)
+		g.refusal(t, &gate, g.actors[1], budgetTestExecution(1), "ACCESS_DENIED")
+		p.UserAccess = BudgetAccessEnabled
+		p.WindowEnd = p.WindowStart
+		g.policy.Store(&p)
+		g.refusal(t, &gate, g.actors[1], budgetTestExecution(1), "SERVICE_NOT_READY")
+		p.WindowEnd = p.WindowStart.Add(-time.Hour)
+		p.WindowStart = p.WindowEnd.Add(-time.Hour)
+		g.policy.Store(&p)
+		g.refusal(t, &gate, g.actors[1], budgetTestExecution(1), "SERVICE_NOT_READY")
+		p.WindowStart = time.Now().UTC().Truncate(time.Hour).Add(24 * time.Hour)
+		p.WindowEnd = p.WindowStart.Add(time.Hour)
+		g.policy.Store(&p)
+		g.refusal(t, &gate, g.actors[1], budgetTestExecution(1), "SERVICE_NOT_READY")
+		var count int
+		if err := g.f.PostgreSQL.QueryRow(g.ctx, `SELECT (SELECT count(*) FROM product_agent_budget_reservations)+(SELECT count(*) FROM product_agent_budget_installations)+(SELECT count(*) FROM product_agent_budget_users)`).Scan(&count); err != nil || count != 0 {
+			t.Fatalf("refused policy changed durable state: %d, %v", count, err)
+		}
+		g.reset(t)
+		if result, err := gate.Reserve(g.ctx, g.actors[1], budgetTestExecution(0)); err != nil || result.State != BudgetNew {
+			t.Fatalf("policy recovery: %+v, %v", result, err)
+		}
+		g.counters("", BudgetCeiling{1, 0}, 1)
+	})
+
+	t.Run("user capacity spans authorized workspaces", func(t *testing.T) {
+		g.reset(t)
+		p := *g.policy.Load()
+		p.User = BudgetCeiling{1, 10}
+		g.policy.Store(&p)
+		workspace := uuid.NewString()
+		g.exec(`INSERT INTO workspaces(id,tenant_id,name,status) VALUES($1,$2,'Budget second workspace','active')`, workspace, g.f.Tenant)
+		g.exec(`INSERT INTO workspace_memberships(user_id,tenant_id,workspace_id,role,authority_id) VALUES($1,$2,$3,'owner',$4)`, g.f.User, g.f.Tenant, workspace, uuid.NewString())
+		if result, err := g.gates[0].Reserve(g.ctx, g.actors[1], budgetTestExecution(1)); err != nil || result.State != BudgetNew {
+			t.Fatalf("first workspace admission: %+v, %v", result, err)
+		}
+		other := g.actors[1]
+		other.Me.Workspace = &identity.Workspace{ID: workspace, TenantID: g.f.Tenant}
+		g.refusal(t, g.gates[1], other, budgetTestExecution(1), "RATE_LIMITED")
+		g.counters(g.f.User, BudgetCeiling{1, 1}, 1)
+	})
+
+	t.Run("rollback and unknown commit preserve authority", func(t *testing.T) {
+		g.reset(t)
+		execution := budgetTestExecution(7)
+		rollback := g.gate(&budgetOutcomeStore{Store: g.f.Store, rollback: true})
+		g.refusal(t, rollback, g.actors[1], execution, "STORAGE_UNAVAILABLE")
+		unknown := g.gate(&budgetOutcomeStore{Store: g.f.Store})
+		g.refusal(t, unknown, g.actors[1], execution, "STORAGE_COMMIT_OUTCOME_UNKNOWN")
+		g.counters("", BudgetCeiling{1, 7}, 1)
+		// A new service and independent pool recover the hold, not execution authority.
+		if result, err := g.gates[1].Reserve(g.ctx, g.actors[1], execution); err != nil || result.State != BudgetHeld {
+			t.Fatalf("reopened unknown admission: %+v, %v", result, err)
+		}
+		settlement := BudgetSettlement{ID: execution.ID, ActualTokens: 2, ReceiptSHA256: strings.Repeat("e", 64)}
+		if result, err := unknown.Settle(g.ctx, g.actors[1], settlement); result != (BudgetReservation{}) || err == nil || err.Error() != "STORAGE_COMMIT_OUTCOME_UNKNOWN" {
+			t.Fatalf("unknown settlement: %+v, %v", result, err)
+		}
+		if result, err := g.gates[1].Settle(g.ctx, g.actors[1], settlement); err != nil || result.State != BudgetSettled {
+			t.Fatalf("reopened settlement: %+v, %v", result, err)
+		}
+		g.counters("", BudgetCeiling{1, 2}, 1)
+	})
+
+	t.Run("finite integer limits", func(t *testing.T) {
+		g.reset(t)
+		p := *g.policy.Load()
+		p.User = BudgetCeiling{}
+		g.policy.Store(&p)
+		g.refusal(t, g.gates[0], g.actors[1], budgetTestExecution(0), "RATE_LIMITED")
+		p.Installation = BudgetCeiling{math.MaxInt64, math.MaxInt64}
+		p.User = p.Installation
+		g.policy.Store(&p)
+		execution := budgetTestExecution(math.MaxInt64)
+		if result, err := g.gates[0].Reserve(g.ctx, g.actors[1], execution); err != nil || result.State != BudgetNew {
+			t.Fatalf("maximum finite token reservation: %+v, %v", result, err)
+		}
+		g.refusal(t, g.gates[1], g.actors[1], budgetTestExecution(1), "RATE_LIMITED")
+		g.counters("", BudgetCeiling{1, math.MaxInt64}, 1)
+		if result, err := g.gates[0].Settle(g.ctx, g.actors[1], BudgetSettlement{ID: execution.ID, ReceiptSHA256: strings.Repeat("e", 64)}); err != nil || result.State != BudgetSettled {
+			t.Fatalf("maximum unused token refund: %+v, %v", result, err)
+		}
+		g.exec(`UPDATE product_agent_budget_installations SET executions=$1,tokens=0`, int64(math.MaxInt64-1))
+		g.exec(`UPDATE product_agent_budget_users SET executions=$1,tokens=0`, int64(math.MaxInt64-1))
+		if result, err := g.gates[1].Reserve(g.ctx, g.actors[1], budgetTestExecution(0)); err != nil || result.State != BudgetNew {
+			t.Fatalf("maximum finite execution charge: %+v, %v", result, err)
+		}
+		g.refusal(t, g.gates[0], g.actors[1], budgetTestExecution(0), "RATE_LIMITED")
+		g.counters("", BudgetCeiling{math.MaxInt64, 0}, 2)
+	})
+
+	t.Run("settlement retains the original policy window", func(t *testing.T) {
+		g.reset(t)
+		old := *g.policy.Load()
+		execution := budgetTestExecution(7)
+		if result, err := g.gates[0].Reserve(g.ctx, g.actors[1], execution); err != nil || result.State != BudgetNew {
+			t.Fatalf("original admission: %+v, %v", result, err)
+		}
+		next := old
+		next.WindowStart = old.WindowStart.Add(-time.Hour)
+		next.WindowEnd = old.WindowEnd.Add(time.Hour)
+		g.policy.Store(&next)
+		if result, err := g.gates[1].Reserve(g.ctx, g.actors[1], execution); err != nil || result.State != BudgetHeld {
+			t.Fatalf("window change replay: %+v, %v", result, err)
+		}
+		if result, err := g.gates[1].Reserve(g.ctx, g.actors[1], budgetTestExecution(5)); err != nil || result.State != BudgetNew {
+			t.Fatalf("next window admission: %+v, %v", result, err)
+		}
+		settlement := BudgetSettlement{ID: execution.ID, ActualTokens: 2, ReceiptSHA256: strings.Repeat("f", 64)}
+		// Settlement is permitted even when new execution is explicitly disabled.
+		next.UserAccess = BudgetAccessDisabled
+		g.policy.Store(&next)
+		if result, err := g.gates[0].Settle(g.ctx, g.actors[1], settlement); err != nil || result.State != BudgetSettled {
+			t.Fatalf("original window settlement: %+v, %v", result, err)
+		}
+		g.counters("", BudgetCeiling{1, 5}, 2)
+		g.policy.Store(&old)
+		g.counters("", BudgetCeiling{1, 2}, 2)
+		g.counters(g.f.User, BudgetCeiling{1, 2}, 2)
+	})
+
+	t.Run("cancellation while waiting for shared capacity", func(t *testing.T) {
+		g.reset(t)
+		if _, err := g.gates[0].Reserve(g.ctx, g.actors[1], budgetTestExecution(1)); err != nil {
+			t.Fatal(err)
+		}
+		blocker, err := g.f.PostgreSQL.Begin(g.ctx)
+		if err != nil {
+			t.Fatal(err)
+		}
+		defer blocker.Rollback(g.ctx)
+		var blockerID uint32
+		if err := blocker.QueryRow(g.ctx, `SELECT pg_backend_pid()`).Scan(&blockerID); err != nil {
+			t.Fatal(err)
+		}
+		if _, err := blocker.Exec(g.ctx, `SELECT executions FROM product_agent_budget_installations FOR UPDATE`); err != nil {
+			t.Fatal(err)
+		}
+		ctx, cancel := context.WithCancel(g.ctx)
+		defer cancel()
+		finished := make(chan budgetTestOutcome, 1)
+		go func() {
+			r, err := g.gates[1].Reserve(ctx, g.actors[2], budgetTestExecution(3))
+			finished <- budgetTestOutcome{r, err}
+		}()
+		poll, stop := context.WithTimeout(g.ctx, 2*time.Second)
+		defer stop()
+		ticker := time.NewTicker(10 * time.Millisecond)
+		defer ticker.Stop()
+		blocked := false
+		for !blocked && poll.Err() == nil {
+			if err := g.f.PostgreSQL.QueryRow(poll, `SELECT EXISTS(SELECT 1 FROM pg_stat_activity WHERE application_name=$1 AND $2=ANY(pg_blocking_pids(pid)))`,
+				g.replicaPool.Config().ConnConfig.RuntimeParams["application_name"], blockerID).Scan(&blocked); err != nil {
+				break
+			}
+			if !blocked {
+				select {
+				case <-ticker.C:
+				case <-poll.Done():
+				}
+			}
+		}
+		cancel()
+		result := <-finished
+		if !blocked || result.reservation != (BudgetReservation{}) || !errors.Is(result.err, context.Canceled) {
+			t.Fatalf("locked cancellation: blocked=%v, result=%+v, error=%v", blocked, result.reservation, result.err)
+		}
+		if err := blocker.Rollback(g.ctx); err != nil {
+			t.Fatal(err)
+		}
+		g.counters("", BudgetCeiling{1, 1}, 1)
+	})
+
+	t.Run("missing candidate schema fails closed then recovers", func(t *testing.T) {
+		g.reset(t)
+		execution := budgetTestExecution(3)
+		g.exec(`ALTER TABLE product_agent_budget_reservations RENAME TO product_agent_budget_reservations_unavailable`)
+		g.refusal(t, g.gates[0], g.actors[1], execution, "STORAGE_UNAVAILABLE")
+		g.exec(`ALTER TABLE product_agent_budget_reservations_unavailable RENAME TO product_agent_budget_reservations`)
+		if result, err := g.gates[1].Reserve(g.ctx, g.actors[1], execution); err != nil || result.State != BudgetNew {
+			t.Fatalf("schema recovery: %+v, %v", result, err)
+		}
+		g.counters("", BudgetCeiling{1, 3}, 1)
+	})
+
+	t.Run("authority denial precedes policy and reservation", func(t *testing.T) {
+		g.reset(t)
+		var calls atomic.Int64
+		gate := *g.gates[0]
+		gate.policy = func(context.Context, transaction.Executor, BudgetSubject) (ExecutionBudgetPolicy, error) {
+			calls.Add(1)
+			return *g.policy.Load(), nil
+		}
+		foreignTenant, foreignWorkspace := uuid.NewString(), uuid.NewString()
+		g.exec(`INSERT INTO tenants(id,name,status) VALUES($1,'Budget foreign tenant','active')`, foreignTenant)
+		g.exec(`INSERT INTO workspaces(id,tenant_id,name,status) VALUES($1,$2,'Budget foreign workspace','active')`, foreignWorkspace, foreignTenant)
+		foreign := g.actors[1]
+		foreign.Me.Workspace = &identity.Workspace{ID: foreignWorkspace, TenantID: foreignTenant}
+		g.refusal(t, &gate, foreign, budgetTestExecution(1), "RESOURCE_NOT_FOUND")
+		g.exec(`DELETE FROM workspace_memberships WHERE user_id=$1 AND workspace_id=$2`, g.actors[2].Me.User.ID, g.f.Workspace)
+		g.refusal(t, &gate, g.actors[2], budgetTestExecution(1), "RESOURCE_NOT_FOUND")
+		g.exec(`UPDATE sessions SET revoked_at=clock_timestamp(),revoke_reason='logout' WHERE id=$1`, g.actors[1].SessionID)
+		g.refusal(t, &gate, g.actors[1], budgetTestExecution(1), "AUTH_SESSION_EXPIRED")
+		if calls.Load() != 0 {
+			t.Fatal("unavailable authority reached the trusted budget policy")
+		}
+		var count int
+		if err := g.f.PostgreSQL.QueryRow(g.ctx, `SELECT count(*) FROM product_agent_budget_reservations`).Scan(&count); err != nil || count != 0 {
+			t.Fatalf("denied authority left reservations: %d, %v", count, err)
+		}
+	})
+}
+
+func (g *budgetRepositoryFixture) refusal(t *testing.T, gate *ExecutionBudgets, actor identity.Auth, execution BudgetExecution, code string) {
+	t.Helper()
+	result, err := gate.Reserve(g.ctx, actor, execution)
+	if result != (BudgetReservation{}) || err == nil || err.Error() != code {
+		t.Fatalf("refusal: %+v, %v; want %s", result, err, code)
+	}
+}
+
+// The callback executes on PostgreSQL. The wrapper injects a lost reply only
+// after a real commit, or a failure inside the callback to force a real rollback.
+type budgetOutcomeStore struct {
+	transaction.Store
+	rollback bool
+}
+
+func (s *budgetOutcomeStore) Within(ctx context.Context, readOnly bool, fn func(context.Context, transaction.Executor) error) error {
+	err := s.Store.Within(ctx, readOnly, func(ctx context.Context, tx transaction.Executor) error {
+		if err := fn(ctx, tx); err != nil {
+			return err
+		}
+		if s.rollback {
+			return &transaction.Error{Kind: transaction.Unavailable}
+		}
+		return nil
+	})
+	if err != nil {
+		return err
+	}
+	return &transaction.Error{Kind: transaction.CommitUnknown}
+}
diff --git a/services/control/internal/modules/productagent/execution_budget_test.go b/services/control/internal/modules/productagent/execution_budget_test.go
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..0e03f9cf
--- /dev/null
+++ b/services/control/internal/modules/productagent/execution_budget_test.go
@@ -0,0 +1,104 @@
+package productagent
+
+import (
+	"context"
+	"math"
+	"strings"
+	"testing"
+	"time"
+
+	"github.com/Passion-Flow/ownsolid/services/control/internal/modules/identity"
+	"github.com/google/uuid"
+)
+
+func TestExecutionBudgetBoundaries(t *testing.T) {
+	for _, tc := range []struct {
+		name          string
+		used, ceiling BudgetCeiling
+		tokens        int64
+		want          bool
+	}{
+		{"zero executions", BudgetCeiling{}, BudgetCeiling{Tokens: 1}, 0, false},
+		{"deterministic command", BudgetCeiling{}, BudgetCeiling{Executions: 1}, 0, true},
+		{"no model allowance", BudgetCeiling{}, BudgetCeiling{Executions: 1}, 1, false},
+		{"exact token capacity", BudgetCeiling{1, 2}, BudgetCeiling{2, 5}, 3, true},
+		{"execution exhausted", BudgetCeiling{2, 2}, BudgetCeiling{2, 5}, 1, false},
+		{"lowered token ceiling", BudgetCeiling{1, 5}, BudgetCeiling{2, 4}, 0, false},
+		{"maximum token charge", BudgetCeiling{}, BudgetCeiling{math.MaxInt64, math.MaxInt64}, math.MaxInt64, true},
+		{"token overflow denied", BudgetCeiling{1, math.MaxInt64}, BudgetCeiling{math.MaxInt64, math.MaxInt64}, 1, false},
+		{"execution overflow denied", BudgetCeiling{math.MaxInt64, 0}, BudgetCeiling{math.MaxInt64, math.MaxInt64}, 0, false},
+		{"negative stored usage", BudgetCeiling{1, -1}, BudgetCeiling{2, 5}, 1, false},
+		{"negative charge", BudgetCeiling{}, BudgetCeiling{2, 5}, -1, false},
+	} {
+		t.Run(tc.name, func(t *testing.T) {
+			if got := budgetFits(tc.used, tc.ceiling, tc.tokens); got != tc.want {
+				t.Fatalf("capacity decision %v, want %v", got, tc.want)
+			}
+		})
+	}
+}
+
+func TestExecutionBudgetPolicyRequiresCompleteExplicitWindow(t *testing.T) {
+	start := time.Date(2026, 11, 12, 0, 0, 0, 0, time.UTC)
+	valid := ExecutionBudgetPolicy{UserAccess: BudgetAccessEnabled, WindowStart: start, WindowEnd: start.Add(time.Hour)}
+	if !validBudgetPolicy(valid) {
+		t.Fatal("zero ceilings must be valid finite denial, not an unlimited default")
+	}
+	for _, mutate := range []func(*ExecutionBudgetPolicy){
+		func(p *ExecutionBudgetPolicy) { p.UserAccess = "" },
+		func(p *ExecutionBudgetPolicy) { p.UserAccess = "unknown" },
+		func(p *ExecutionBudgetPolicy) { p.WindowStart = time.Time{} },
+		func(p *ExecutionBudgetPolicy) { p.WindowEnd = p.WindowStart },
+		func(p *ExecutionBudgetPolicy) { p.WindowEnd = p.WindowStart.Add(-time.Hour) },
+		func(p *ExecutionBudgetPolicy) { p.WindowStart = p.WindowStart.Add(time.Nanosecond) },
+		func(p *ExecutionBudgetPolicy) { p.WindowEnd = p.WindowEnd.Add(time.Nanosecond) },
+		func(p *ExecutionBudgetPolicy) { p.Installation.Executions = -1 },
+		func(p *ExecutionBudgetPolicy) { p.Installation.Tokens = -1 },
+		func(p *ExecutionBudgetPolicy) { p.User.Executions = -1 },
+		func(p *ExecutionBudgetPolicy) { p.User.Tokens = -1 },
+	} {
+		p := valid
+		mutate(&p)
+		if validBudgetPolicy(p) {
+			t.Fatalf("incomplete policy admitted: %+v", p)
+		}
+	}
+}
+
+func TestExecutionBudgetRejectsUntrustedRequestBeforeStorage(t *testing.T) {
+	var gate *ExecutionBudgets
+	valid := BudgetExecution{ID: uuid.NewString(), ExecutionSHA256: strings.Repeat("a", 64)}
+	for _, execution := range []BudgetExecution{
+		{},
+		{ID: "client choice", ExecutionSHA256: valid.ExecutionSHA256},
+		{ID: valid.ID, ExecutionSHA256: strings.Repeat("A", 64)},
+		{ID: valid.ID, ExecutionSHA256: strings.Repeat("a", 63)},
+		{ID: valid.ID, ExecutionSHA256: valid.ExecutionSHA256, MaximumTokens: -1},
+	} {
+		result, err := gate.Reserve(t.Context(), identity.Auth{}, execution)
+		if result != (BudgetReservation{}) || err == nil || err.Error() != "VALIDATION_FAILED" {
+			t.Fatalf("malformed execution returned %+v, %v", result, err)
+		}
+	}
+	for _, ctx := range []context.Context{nil, t.Context()} {
+		if result, err := gate.Reserve(ctx, identity.Auth{}, valid); result != (BudgetReservation{}) || err != ErrCommandDenied {
+			t.Fatalf("missing authority returned %+v, %v", result, err)
+		}
+	}
+	if _, err := NewExecutionBudgets(nil, nil); err == nil {
+		t.Fatal("constructed a gate without authority")
+	}
+	for _, settlement := range []BudgetSettlement{
+		{},
+		{ID: valid.ID, ReceiptSHA256: strings.Repeat("c", 63)},
+		{ID: valid.ID, ReceiptSHA256: strings.Repeat("C", 64)},
+		{ID: valid.ID, ActualTokens: -1, ReceiptSHA256: strings.Repeat("c", 64)},
+	} {
+		if result, err := gate.Settle(t.Context(), identity.Auth{}, settlement); result != (BudgetReservation{}) || err == nil || err.Error() != "VALIDATION_FAILED" {
+			t.Fatalf("malformed settlement returned %+v, %v", result, err)
+		}
+	}
+	if result, err := gate.Settle(nil, identity.Auth{}, BudgetSettlement{ID: valid.ID, ReceiptSHA256: valid.ExecutionSHA256}); result != (BudgetReservation{}) || err != ErrCommandDenied {
+		t.Fatalf("settlement without authority returned %+v, %v", result, err)
+	}
+}
diff --git a/services/control/internal/modules/productagent/testdata/execution-budget.sql b/services/control/internal/modules/productagent/testdata/execution-budget.sql
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..943d9feb
--- /dev/null
+++ b/services/control/internal/modules/productagent/testdata/execution-budget.sql
@@ -0,0 +1,43 @@
+-- Candidate AGT-112 schema for isolated repository acceptance only.
+-- Production requires an owned forward migration and restore-catalogue registration.
+CREATE TABLE product_agent_budget_installations (
+    window_start timestamptz NOT NULL,
+    window_end timestamptz NOT NULL,
+    executions bigint NOT NULL DEFAULT 0 CHECK (executions >= 0),
+    tokens bigint NOT NULL DEFAULT 0 CHECK (tokens >= 0),
+    PRIMARY KEY (window_start, window_end),
+    CHECK (window_start < window_end)
+);
+
+CREATE TABLE product_agent_budget_users (
+    user_id uuid NOT NULL,
+    window_start timestamptz NOT NULL,
+    window_end timestamptz NOT NULL,
+    executions bigint NOT NULL DEFAULT 0 CHECK (executions >= 0),
+    tokens bigint NOT NULL DEFAULT 0 CHECK (tokens >= 0),
+    PRIMARY KEY (user_id, window_start, window_end),
+    CHECK (window_start < window_end)
+);
+
+CREATE TABLE product_agent_budget_reservations (
+    id uuid PRIMARY KEY,
+    tenant_id uuid NOT NULL,
+    user_id uuid NOT NULL,
+    workspace_id uuid NOT NULL,
+    audience text NOT NULL CHECK (audience IN ('admin', 'portal')),
+    execution_sha256 text NOT NULL CHECK (execution_sha256 ~ '^[a-f0-9]{64}$'),
+    maximum_tokens bigint NOT NULL CHECK (maximum_tokens >= 0),
+    window_start timestamptz NOT NULL,
+    window_end timestamptz NOT NULL,
+    state text NOT NULL CHECK (state IN ('held', 'settled')),
+    actual_tokens bigint,
+    receipt_sha256 text,
+    CHECK (window_start < window_end),
+    CHECK (
+        (state = 'held' AND actual_tokens IS NULL AND receipt_sha256 IS NULL)
+        OR
+        (state = 'settled' AND actual_tokens IS NOT NULL AND actual_tokens >= 0
+            AND actual_tokens <= maximum_tokens AND receipt_sha256 IS NOT NULL
+            AND receipt_sha256 ~ '^[a-f0-9]{64}$')
+    )
+);
